## Project-wide constraints

- Use `pnpm test` after implementing complex tasks (never pnpm dev)
- Prefer named exports** (`export const foo`) not `export default` for module
- **Throw `Error` objects** never strings (enables proper stack traces)
- Document exported/public APIs and non-trivial code paths with comprehensive JSDoc. Omit for trivial UI components. Include:
    - `@param`, `@returns`, `@throws`
    - Loading/error states for async ops
    - Conditional rendering rationale

## TypeScript strictness
- Enable `strict`, `noImplicitOverride`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`
- Always provide explicit return types on exported functions
